# LABDATA is the root the Makefile mounts the data from. Nothing in the tree
# reads a .env file: set the variable in the shell or on the make command
# line. .env is ignored by git, so a copy of this file edited under that
# name stays out of the tree.
#
# Every declared location <name> is the subdirectory $LABDATA/<name> and
# nothing else: no variable overrides one. These are the paths the Makefile
# mounts them at inside the container:
#
#   $LABDATA/raw           mounted read-only at /data/raw
#   $LABDATA/derived       mounted read-write at /data/derived
#
# A make target that needs LABDATA and finds it unset stops before starting
# the container and says so.
#
# LABDATA is the only variable these two locations come from. Nothing under
# it is ever committed: input data is mounted read-only from outside the tree
# (see docs/data.md). Never point any location inside this repository.
LABDATA=/absolute/path/to/labdata

# The two locations by name. Nothing in the tree reads either variable, so
# setting one moves nothing.
#
#   LAB_RAW       raw input datasets: opened read-only, never written to
#   LAB_DERIVED   derived artifacts: read-write, regenerable, never committed
#
#LAB_RAW=/absolute/path/to/raw
#LAB_DERIVED=/absolute/path/to/derived
